==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology===
Possibly a {{clq|en|sh|etničko čišćenje|nocap=1}}, though this is probably attested later. Originally used of (and still often associated with) the wars in former Yugoslavia during the 1990s.

===Noun===
{{en-noun|-}}

# The [[mass]] [[expulsion]] or [[killing]] of [[people]] belonging to one ethnic [[group]] by those of another.
#* {{quote-web|en|url=http://www.theguardian.com/world/1999/apr/24/alexbrummer.martinkettle1|title=The bombing goes on|date=1999-04-24|author=Martin Kettle; Alex Brummer|work=The Guardian|quotee=w:Tony Blair|passage=These television stations are part of the apparatus and power of Milosevic. This is the apparatus he has used to do the '''ethnic cleansing''' in Kosovo.}}

====Synonyms====
* {{l|en|ethnic purge}} {{q|countable}}

